Marcus starts with his house at 40 degrees. He spends 3 hours baking, and each hour the temperature increases by 5 degrees. So:

$$
\text{Temperature increase from baking} = 3 \text{ hours} \times 5 \text{ degrees/hour} = 15 \text{ degrees}
$$

$$
\text{Temperature after baking} = 40 + 15 = 55 \text{ degrees}
$$

Next, Marcus opens a window for 30 minutes. The house cools down 2 degrees for every 10 minutes the window is open. In 30 minutes, the window is open for:

$$
\frac{30}{10} = 3 \text{ intervals of 10 minutes}
$$

$$
\text{Temperature decrease} = 3 \times 2 = 6 \text{ degrees}
$$

$$
\text{Final temperature} = 55 - 6 = 49 \text{ degrees}
$$

$$
\boxed{49}
$$
